WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.999
Clinic AI Agent. WhatsApp and Messenger appointment automation built with n8n.

00:00:02.999 --> 00:00:08.999
Overview. Patients chat on WhatsApp or Messenger. An AI agent books appointments against the live calendar and logs everything in Google Sheets.

00:00:08.999 --> 00:00:15.999
Step 1 · Message in. Meta webhooks verify, acknowledge instantly (so Meta never times out), then parse each channel's payload into one format.

00:00:15.999 --> 00:00:23.000
Step 2 · AI agent. The agent remembers the conversation and chooses the right booking tool. It never guesses availability: it asks the booking engine.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Step 3 · Tool engine. When Executed by Another Workflow feeds Route by Action: one safe, testable branch per action. Nothing writes data except through here.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Step 4 · Real availability. Clinic hours and treatments come from Google Sheets. Busy times come from Google Calendar FreeBusy. Only truly free slots are offered.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Step 5 · Book safely. The chosen slot is re-validated at the moment of booking. Free: calendar event plus Sheets row. Taken: nearest alternatives, never an error or a clash.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:49.999
Step 6 · Cancel & reschedule. Cancel: find the patient's booking, delete the calendar event, mark the row. Reschedule: validate the new slot first, then move both records together.

00:00:49.999 --> 00:00:55.999
Step 7 · Instant confirmation. Extract Reply, then Which Channel? sends the confirmation by Messenger or WhatsApp: the exact channel the patient used. 24/7, in seconds.

00:00:55.999 --> 00:01:01.999
Real canvas. This is the real n8n canvas: Clinic AI Agent on top, booking sub-workflow below. The same node names you just saw, drawn large.

00:01:01.999 --> 00:01:05.999
Book, reschedule, cancel, check availability and my bookings. Full case study on GitHub.
